      "explanation": "Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.",
      "remediation": "Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.",
      "code_snippet": "**Opening URLs:** on Android, use `adb shell \"am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d '<url>'\"`. The inner quotes keep the URL's `&`. On iOS, `simctl openurl` shows an \"Open in '<app>'?\" prompt for any scheme not yet approved. Approve it first:\n\n```bash\nP=~/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Devices/<udid>/data/Library/Preferences/com.apple.launchservices.schemeapproval.plist\nK=\"com.apple.CoreSimulator.CoreSimulatorBridge--><scheme>\"\n/usr/libexec/PlistBuddy -c \"Set :'$K' <bundle id>\" \"$P\" 2>/dev/null || /usr/libexec/PlistBuddy -c \"Add :'$K' string <bundle id>\" \"$P\"\n```",
      "intent": null,
      "tags": [
        "Rogue Agent"
      ],
